# What Claude Code can and can't do in this project

Claude Code cannot push to git, cannot run destructive database commands, and will ask for approval before modifying more than 5 files.

## Denied (`.claude/settings.json`, deny list)

The deny list blocks the command shapes below. It matches literal text, so a variant can get past it.

- `git push` and `git push *`: `Bash(git push)`, `Bash(git push *)`
- `Bash(git reset --hard *)`, `Bash(git checkout -- *)`, `Bash(git clean *)`
- `Bash(rm -rf *)`, `Bash(rm -r *)`
- `Bash(drop *)`, `Bash(DROP *)`
- `Bash(npx prisma migrate reset *)`, `Bash(npx prisma db push --force-reset)`

Why: each one deletes data, discards work or publishes changes.

## Allowed without asking (allow list)

`Read`, `Edit`, `Write`, `Glob`, `Grep`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build`, `npx prisma generate`, `npx tsc --noEmit`, `git status`, `git diff *`, `git log *`, `git branch`.

Why: they read, check or build. Anything on neither list, curl included, asks a person first.

## Rules Claude Code follows (`.claude/CLAUDE.md`, Safety Rules)

- Never modify .env or .env.local files
- Never modify files in database/migrations/ without explicit approval
- Before making changes to more than 5 files, show the plan and wait for approval
- Never run commands against production databases
- Always run tests after modifying source files
- If a test fails, fix the code. Never modify a test to make it pass.

## Hook

A `PostToolUse` hook on `Write|Edit` scans each written file for `API_KEY`, `SECRET`, `PASSWORD` or `PRIVATE_KEY` and exits 2 with `WARNING: possible credential in file`. It needs `jq`. It flags after the write; the file is already on disk.

## Test procedure

Run the 7 safety tests (chapter 7) after every change to `.claude/settings.json` or `.claude/CLAUDE.md`. The latest results are in `safety-tests.md`, next to this file.

## Environment

`.env` points at a local database only. Never a staging or production URL.
